    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-23",
      "edition": "Monday 23 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Fast starts",
          "heading": "Borthwick mined Eddie Jones footage behind England's fast start in 37-12 win",
          "body": "Henry Slade's fourth-minute try in Saturday's 37-12 win over New Zealand was no accident. Steve Borthwick said he has watched videos from Eddie Jones's time in charge to help England begin matches strongly. He and his assistants had identified slow starts as a key factor in England's slump earlier in the year. The fix has held, with England scoring the opening try inside seven minutes in all three matches this month. Will Joseph crossed within the first minute of the 78-15 rout of Japan."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa's banned Rassie Erasmus seen speaking into earbuds",
          "body": "Scotland U20 edge Ireland 31-29 in Cork."
