      }
    },
    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-23",
      "edition": "Monday 23 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "New marksman",
          "heading": "Kalvin Gourgues kicks 5 from 6 on goal-kicking bow in 45-17 win",
          "body": "The 21-year-old centre also scored twice against the Pumas on Saturday. He was handed the tee despite never having kicked at international level, and he had kicked only once in the Top 14. Fabien Galthié explained that France had set off without a recognised goal-kicker, joking that Gourgues had now lost his 100% record. Antoine Dupont, his Toulouse teammate, said the responsibility had not unsettled him. Gourgues admitted he loves kicking and has been practising after sessions with Maxime Petitjean and the other kickers."
        },
        {
