    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-23",
      "edition": "Monday 23 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Attack analysis",
          "heading": "The42 credits Ireland's bold passing against Springbok blitz in 20-17 win",
          "body": "Andy Farrell's side pushed passes into South Africa's linespeed rather than shying away from it, The42's analysis argues, and the tone was set on Saturday's first attack. Off a three-man pod, Ryan Baird swept the ball out the back to Sam Prendergast, whose dummy to Robbie Henshaw held up Cameron Hanekom before he released the centre through Morné van den Berg's grasp into the South Africa 22. On the very next phase, Jamison Gibson-Park fizzed a pass across Prendergast's face to buy Stuart McCloskey time."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa's banned Rassie Erasmus seen speaking into earbuds",
