    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-23",
      "edition": "Monday 23 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "U20 result",
          "heading": "Scotland U20 edge Ireland 31-29 in Cork as Dalrymple and Caldwell score",
          "body": "Scotland U20 owed Friday's win at Musgrave Park to steadier goal-kicking, overcoming an Ireland side who scored five tries behind a dominant scrum and maul. Ireland crossed twice while centre Harry Soboil was in the bin, but their own indiscipline brought cards for Jonny Ginnety and Bernard White, and Scotland struck through wing Rory Caldwell, second row James Dalrymple and lock Christian Lindsay. Ireland's Paul Neary then watched a late conversion that would have levelled it drift wide."
        },
