      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coach backed",
          "heading": "New Zealand Rugby backs Dave Rennie after 37-12 England defeat at Twickenham",
          "body": "The union has publicly stood by its head coach after successive defeats by Wales and England. The second, a 37-12 loss, was the most points the All Blacks have conceded in a Test against a Northern Hemisphere nation. Rennie conceded his team were 'miles off' and that London was worse than Cardiff. In the Herald, Gregor Paul recalled that last year's defeat by England ultimately led to Scott Robertson's removal. The All Blacks now face England again at Twickenham in the Nations Championship third-place final."
        },
